Musica Administrative Utilities
===============================

Purpose
-------
The admin/ directory contains low-level maintenance and administrative
utilities for the Musica database environment. These tools are intended
for system administrators or advanced users who need to perform direct
maintenance or validation outside normal day-to-day operations.

Contents
--------
cleanup.csh       - Performs deep cleanup of temporary, log, or residual
                    files left by test or import/export operations.
                    Use with care.

backup_db.csh     - Creates a full backup of the current Musica database
                    and stores it under ./data/archive/ with a timestamped
                    filename.

restore_db.csh    - Restores the database from a selected backup created
                    by backup_db.csh.

verify_env.csh    - Performs environment validation: checks for correct
                    directory structure, permissions, config file presence,
                    and database service availability.

Usage Notes
-----------
- These scripts should NOT be used in routine operation or by casual users.
- All scripts assume the configuration file config/musica.conf is properly
  defined and readable.
- Run scripts from within their directory, or ensure $PATH includes the
  admin/ directory.
- Most actions require elevated privileges (sudo), particularly those
  involving database service control or data restoration.

Examples
--------
  cd /opt/musica/admin
  sudo ./verify_env.csh
  sudo ./backup_db.csh
  sudo ./cleanup.csh

Safety Warning
--------------
- Do NOT modify or remove data directly from the database or data/ tree
  without a verified backup.
- cleanup.csh and restore_db.csh can cause irreversible data loss if misused.
- Always test changes in a non-production environment first.

